id: pm-linear-field-ownership
title: Preview Linear field ownership and same-field conflicts
description: Compare an explicitly acknowledged Linear field snapshot with complete SDK local reads and current provider observations. Read-only preview; no cross-system atomic guarantee.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T09:23:36.129Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T20:13:11.973Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Disjoint edits are distinguished from same-field conflicts; unknown bases never imply safe overwrites; preview makes zero mutations and explicitly declines atomic cross-system guarantees; typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON, actionable refusals, docs, seeded model tests and public tracker validation."
comments[34]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T09:23:55.309Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: host SDK exposes threeWayFieldConflict and complete SDK reads; Linear negotiateLinearSchema detects metadata drift while syncLinearIssues upserts values. ADO sync/resolution owns revision-test writes. Jira mappings have no Linear ownership preview. This feature reuses SDK conflict decisions and existing Linear projections, isolates local reads, and adds observational context only. Installed pinned SDK is 2026.10.20; current registry CLI is 2026.10.27, with no dependency bump planned."
  "2026-10-27T09:24:04.444Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: SDK threeWayFieldConflict and complete SDK reads cover core comparison and acquisition. Linear negotiateLinearSchema detects metadata drift; syncLinearIssues upserts values. ADO sync/resolution owns revision-test writes; Jira has no Linear ownership preview. This adds observational context only. Pinned SDK is 2026.10.20; registry CLI is 2026.10.27, with no pin bump planned."
  "2026-10-27T09:30:26.778Z",codex-agent,"Implemented read-only ownership preview with isolated SDK complete reads, SDK canonicalDocument normalization, role-based status mapping and existing due-date projection. No create/update/apply path or package journal is introduced. Baselines are explicit operator-acknowledged observation artifacts, scoped by item/provider identity and mapping. Invalid/duplicate field records fail alone as unknown. Correction to overlap note: threeWayFieldConflict is ADO package logic, not a core SDK export. Targeted tests caught timestamp-versus-date drift; both sides now use the existing export-date projection."
  "2026-10-27T09:37:41.613Z",codex-agent,"Public immutable-copy validation: 109 real items; original unlinked selection refused before network (0 requests). A separately declared one-item synthetic overlay produced disjoint local/provider edits (1/1), 0 unknowns, 1 same-field conflict, 6 total read requests, and a 2542-byte JSON receipt. Source hashes unchanged during previews; live Linear is not claimed. Behavioral revert proof: replacing only the new classification with two-way equality failed the known-bases regression (expected 8 unknown fields, observed 0); source restored."
  "2026-10-27T09:47:17.410Z",codex-agent,"Boundary checks passed individually: 4 initial targeted tests, 2 custom-status/isolation tests, and installed-host-link regression. Combined linked-test run hit its 120-second runner timeout under host contention after 2 passing tests; no assertion failure occurred and it is missing full evidence, not approval. Full release gates remain delegated to npm/Bun CI at unchanged thresholds. Inherited atomic import replay probe confirmed same transaction/recovered=true despite a newer differing SDK target; recorded separately as pm-linear-atomic-replay-revision. Ownership preview has no write/recovery path."
  "2026-10-27T09:54:28.284Z",codex-agent,"Linked tests rerun with explicit 600-second timeout: 7 tests passed, 0 failed, in 88 seconds. Separate prototype-shaped key test passed; reverting only parseStatusMap own-property insertion made it fail, then source was restored. Source classification revert likewise failed the known-bases regression. Model test contains 500 seeded sequences and is included in CI; local long attempt was canceled under shared-host contention and is not counted as passed. No dedicated lint script exists; typecheck, test typecheck, docstring gate and diff check passed."
  "2026-10-27T09:55:13.927Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance passed all 5 isolated host modes: project-local npm, npm global symlink, Bun global, npx and bunx; each made 2 provider reads and returned all 8 unknown fields without a baseline. Supported lazy SDK loading uses host-installed SDK linkage, never argv/which/symlink path inference. Exact report: docs/field-ownership-packed.json. Installed runtime SDK links are excluded from source data copies; foreign item symlinks still refuse. Ready for review with full npm/Bun CI gate evidence pending; inherited replay follow-up remains open."
  "2026-10-27T10:03:18.303Z",codex-agent,"CI run 40484745175 is queued with no gate counts. Reviewed the seeded reference model while waiting: omitted assignee/deadline values now replace mapped fields rather than inheriting current local values, and provider replay sequences include null deadlines. A temporary 20-sequence diagnostic sample passed; this does not replace the required 500-sequence release suite. Production code is unchanged by this oracle correction."
  "2026-10-27T10:21:18.975Z",codex-agent,"Release-gate evidence remains pending: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40485647905 at source/test head e469b45 has npm, Bun and both Node jobs queued; no full-suite pass counts are available. The first-push CI wait is capped at 30 minutes by the queue rules. Local strict health exits 1 with the same finding classes/severities as an isolated origin/main copy: extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (gate-failing) and provenance_value_domain_invalid (advisory), already tracked by pm-linear-bzam and pm-linear-jloc. Both changed history streams preserve their main prefixes. Additional overlap verification inspected all 377 public SDK declaration files in CLI 2026.10.26; its pure document/JSON merge helpers have preferred-side/collection merge semantics and are not used as a Linear write or ownership guarantee. Production code remains unchanged since 5f09574; 500-sequence property and full npm/Bun gate evidence must be obtained in CI. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/183. Items remain open and the feature claim is released."
  "2026-10-27T10:30:17.718Z",codex-agent,"Final test typecheck caught a declaration-only issue in the corrected reference model: Object.fromEntries erased required SDK metadata fields from its inferred type. The model now explicitly carries type, created_at and updated_at from SDK read-back; runtime values are unchanged. npm run build:test now passes at the corrected test source. CI remained queued through the 30-minute wait cap, with 0 of 2 full release gates completed and no pass counts. Superseded queued runs will be canceled; the PR links the latest head checks. Production code remains unchanged, items are unclosed, and the feature claim remains released."
  "2026-10-27T10:49:34.672Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 1: all four findings accepted. General classes: one source of truth for provider-to-local mapping; provider schemas match nullable/optional API domains; validate entire baseline including duplicate identities before trusting any row; validate GraphQL envelopes before dereferencing. Merged the newer main release first. Audit covers all request consumers, schema/thread/closure/import/export commands, SDK and CLI render paths, baseline ingestion and packed non-git consumers. Will add adversarial/property coverage and per-class behavioral revert proofs, then run serial npm/Bun full gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-27T12:03:24.777Z",codex-agent,"Re-review fixes close four classes: preview now calls the import mapper and SDK canonicalizer; import/ownership share nullable issue schemas; the entire baseline is validated before any authority is returned; every HTTP consumer validates the envelope before dereference and preserves typed source_invalid field diagnostics through JSON/TOON dispatch. The package-wide lookup audit also hardened prototype-shaped mapping keys and skips ambiguous current Linear identities in both writers. Behavioral reverts fail for independent status mapping (conflict witness), nullable cycle schema (valid response refused), malformed duplicate baseline handling (unknown_base assertion), unchecked envelopes (typed-refusal assertion), and inherited-property lookup (mapping assertion). Restored production source after each revert; no tests weakened. Focused shared dispatch/preflight/container tests: 3 passed; typecheck, test typecheck and 88-declaration docstring gate passed. Full serial npm/Bun gates and refreshed packed/public-copy evidence follow."
  "2026-10-27T12:16:31.669Z",codex-agent,"Focused re-review linked test run passed 10/10 (328 seconds), including all-field malformed duplicate permutations, nullable/omitted provider objects, SDK/CLI consumers and preflight. Additional focused legacy empty-body/tag application and malformed create/update acknowledgements passed 2/2; the latter report write_unconfirmed instead of confirming malformed responses. A temporary 20-sequence diagnostic against the real atomic dry-run oracle passed; permanent model remains 500 sequences. Broader network/schema run had 91/92 pass with one old viewer-message expectation; that expectation now requires the stronger source_invalid field diagnostic, and its focused rerun passed. Public immutable-copy refresh: 109 items; original selection 0 requests; one-item synthetic overlay, 8 fields, 6 reads, 2542 JSON bytes, disjoint 1/1 and 1 same-field conflict, hashes unchanged. Starting serial full npm/Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds with one test worker."
  "2026-10-27T12:23:20.989Z",codex-agent,"Expanded packed dispatch caught an inherited alias registration mismatch: linear-sync import handled all import options but advertised only schema-version, so the strict host parser rejected team/atomic/dry-run before the handler. Fixed the class by sharing one complete flag definition across both import aliases. Registry regression passes; reverting that definition in an isolated source copy fails the SDK flag assertion. Additional isolated behavioral reverts proved the real importer status projection, empty legacy update fields and import-page container validation (all fail expected assertions). Earlier full npm attempt was stopped early to include this production fix; it is not counted as a gate pass. Restarting unchanged serial npm/Bun gates after the focused registry pass; expanded five-mode packed acceptance is rerunning."
  "2026-10-27T12:47:19.345Z",codex-agent,"Expanded packed acceptance passed 5/5: project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx. Every mode used the pinned 2026.10.20 host SDK with package 2026.10.27, accepted nullable cycles, reported the status conflict, quarantined malformed duplicate baselines and preserved source_invalid/field/exit 2 in JSON and TOON across seven provider command surfaces. Each mode made 23 read requests, covered 14 source-refusal dispatches and emitted a 3221-byte host JSON receipt; no provider mutation request was sent. Report: docs/field-ownership-packed.json. Full npm gate remains active on its 10,001-item corpus test; no failure reported so far."
  "2026-10-27T13:29:46.014Z",codex-agent,"Full local npm attempt passed the 10,002-item complete SDK corpus export/match test and exposed one stale closure assertion: malformed JSON now correctly refuses with source_invalid at response rather than returning an unavailable frontier. Strengthened that assertion, retained all HTTP/no-retry checks and proved the corrected focused test passes (1/1). Added malformed/oversized status-map boundary cases; focused boundary test and test typecheck pass. Stopped the incomplete local full attempt to follow the original saturated-host instruction: full npm/Bun release evidence will come from CI, with at most two one-worker jobs. No full local gate pass is claimed. Production source remains df8f7e9; remaining changes strengthen tests only."
  "2026-10-27T13:45:49.695Z",codex-agent,"Current-source CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40512915488 at 539b5b6. All four jobs remain queued, including both npm/Bun release gates; 0/2 full gates completed and pass counts unavailable. Prior-head success is not current-source evidence. The corrected closure refusal/no-retry regression also passed through pm test (1/1); linked ownership test timeouts are now explicit (600/900 seconds) after the earlier host-load timeout. Final static refresh passed 88-declaration docstrings, test typecheck, changelog check and whitespace check. No local full test process remains running."
  "2026-10-27T13:51:27.405Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding timeout note: both raw JSON edits of existing linked-test timeout metadata were refused by the guarded-item-format check because the project peer range starts at 2026.10.4. No 600/900-second stored timeout update was applied to those two existing links. Their successful runs used the explicit runner --timeout 600. The newly added closure link carries its accepted 600-second timeout and its pm test run passed. Dependency pins and existing history are preserved; no format migration or history repair was attempted. This optional tracker-CLI limitation does not affect ownership runtime behavior."
  "2026-10-27T14:27:39.929Z",codex-agent,"Class audit found and reproduced an additional apply-input mismatch: SDK canonicalDocument keeps a literal none tag, while the old comma-joined update input clears it; comma-containing labels are also split by that transport. Both import writers now use the SDK-documented JSON-array tag input, not a second normalization implementation. All tag payloads use one serializer, empty create bodies/tags are explicit, and both creation paths unset ambient parent/scope defaults. Focused validation passed 4/4, including 500 generated producer inputs checked through SDK parseTags/canonicalDocument, real SDK read-back after atomic/legacy updates, and creates under each actual writer author focus. The permanent 500-operation ownership model now varies control-word, delimiter and Unicode labels. The first push CI wait cap elapsed with jobs still queued; no further CI waiting will be added while final independent regression/packed work completes."
  "2026-10-27T15:13:17.661Z",codex-agent,"Final permanent model passed: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"500 seeded operation sequences\" test/ownership.test.ts — 1 test passed, 0 failed; 500 seeded operation sequences completed in 1718.6 seconds (1731.6 seconds total). It compares every preview field to a real atomic dry-run import plan and reads native state back through the SDK, including replayed inputs/bases, CRLF/whitespace, all mapped fields, literal control/delimiter labels, relationships, ambient focus and random status registries. Additional 500 tag-producer cases and real atomic/legacy update/create read-backs passed; final focused atomic/tag sweep 4/4, linked tag test 1/1, linked closure 1/1 and prior linked review sweep 10/10. All 11 isolated behavioral reverts failed as expected, including tag JSON input and both focus-safe creation paths. Final packed rerun passed 5/5 with 23 reads and 14 JSON/TOON refusal dispatches per mode; public-copy refresh remains 109 original items, 0 original requests, one synthetic overlay, 8 fields, 6 reads, 2542 compact JSON bytes, independent edits 1/1 and one same-field conflict, immutable hashes unchanged. Full release gates remain CI-only evidence; no incomplete local full attempt or older-head CI success is counted as a current full-gate pass. CI waiting stopped at the first-push cap while independent required model work completed. No merge or release."
  "2026-10-27T15:22:25.341Z",codex-agent,"Final CI inspection of source head 539b5b6 found 400/400 tests passed on npm and Node 22, but the unchanged function threshold failed at 99.50% (lines 99.63%, branches 96.86%). Full-gate success is not claimed. Reclaimed the item to identify the single unexercised function. A local V8 function-coverage diagnostic is running with the already-proved 10,002-item stress case and two 500-state loops excluded from this diagnostic only; release-gate scripts and all thresholds remain unchanged. Added a must-allow viewer optional-object case. Current 500-operation ownership model, final packed modes, real-data copy, tag/writer/focus checks and all 11 behavioral reverts are already passed."
  "2026-10-27T15:31:05.068Z",codex-agent,"Coverage diagnosis: the new offline linked-item filter was never invoked because existing dry-run fixtures contained zero items, even though full CI passed 400 tests. Added a non-git tracker containing linked active and terminal items plus an unlinked item; all three offline command/import aliases report exactly two linked items in JSON and native output, make zero provider requests, and retain SDK-read native state. Focused optional-viewer plus offline-count checks passed 2/2; V8 confirms the predicate is now invoked. The broad local coverage diagnostic was deliberately interrupted after identifying this gap; it is not a full-gate pass. A fresh fetch found main toolchain update b96a587; merging it next, then checking the final SDK pin. Existing 500-operation and five packed-mode receipts used SDK 2026.10.20 and remain explicitly version-scoped."
  "2026-10-27T15:35:38.371Z",codex-agent,"Main toolchain update b96a587 merged as c87ebe2 after code commit da20d64; no PM history overlap required reconciliation. The repository now pins SDK, changelog and ops 2026.10.23. Production/test typecheck and docstrings pass on that pin (88 declarations, 8 files). Packed acceptance now derives the exact host package from the repository pin and strips inherited credential variables before package-manager subprocesses. The Node test-name exclusion also matched its file ancestor, so the current ownership run includes the full permanent 500-operation model; this larger run is being allowed to complete. The earlier interrupted diagnostic never reached either stress/model file and is not full-gate evidence."
  "2026-10-27T15:39:11.132Z",codex-agent,"Completed superseded CI evidence: run 40512915488 at 539b5b6 has all four jobs finished. npm release gate, Bun release gate, Node 22 and Node 26 each passed 400 tests with zero failures, then failed the unchanged 100% function threshold at 99.50% (lines 99.63%, branches 96.86%). Thus 0/2 release gates passed at that head. The new non-empty offline count test invokes the previously unexercised filter 18 times; final-head gate confirmation remains required. The final SDK 2026.10.23 ownership suite is progressing through all 500 operations without a failure so far."
  "2026-10-27T15:45:58.891Z",codex-agent,"Permanent model passed again on the merged SDK 2026.10.23 pin: all 500 seeded operations, zero failures, 737.6 seconds for the model. Current suite continues through the remaining adversarial cases before refreshing public-copy and packed receipts. The newly linked optional-viewer/offline-count command passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress (2 tests passed, zero failures). Reverting only the offline linked-item predicate in an isolated copy made its test fail (3 instead of 2); fixed source remains unchanged, giving twelve behavioral revert proofs total."
  "2026-10-27T15:52:05.983Z",codex-agent,"Merged-pin ownership suite completed: 24 tests passed, zero failed/canceled/skipped, 1034.1 seconds total. Exact invocation: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"^(?!.*500 seeded operation sequences).*$\" test/ownership.test.ts. Node matched the ancestor test, so all 24 tests ran, including the permanent 500-operation model (737.6 seconds) and 500 tag-producer inputs plus real atomic/legacy update/create read-backs. Added the positive model selector as its reproducible 1800-second linked command (the same selector previously passed standalone on SDK 2026.10.20). New viewer/offline-count link also passed through the PM runner on SDK 2026.10.23. Public immutable-copy and packed refreshes follow this successful suite."
  "2026-10-27T16:01:33.887Z",codex-agent,"Final merged-pin acceptance passed on SDK 2026.10.23: ownership suite 24/24 including the permanent 500-operation model, 500 generated tag payloads and real read-backs through both writers; linked viewer/offline check 2/2; all twelve isolated behavioral reverts failed as expected. Public immutable copy: 109 items, original unlinked selection refused before requests, one declared synthetic link/provider overlay, eight fields, six reads, 2542 compact JSON bytes, independent edits 1/1 with zero unknowns, one same-field conflict, 26349 ms measured preview, unchanged original and derived source hashes. Packed artifact acceptance passed project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx (5/5), each with 23 reads and 14 JSON/TOON source-refusal dispatches; host JSON 3221 bytes. Live Linear is not claimed. Production/test typecheck, build, 88-declaration docstrings and whitespace checks passed. No thresholds or existing tests were weakened. Superseded CI has four 400/400 passing test suites but 0/2 release gates passed because of the 99.50% function threshold; the uncovered predicate now has a real non-empty fixture and V8 invocation proof. Final-head CI is still required. The inherited atomic recovery follow-up remains open; this preview has no apply/recovery state."
  "2026-10-27T16:02:30.898Z",codex-agent,"Pushed final source/test/artifact head 7180aeb. Exact-source CI run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40536897541 — queued at inspection; 0/2 npm/Bun release gates completed and no full-suite counts yet. The prior CI run 40512915488 failed only the unchanged function threshold after 400/400 tests in each of four jobs; the real non-empty predicate test and all current-pin local proofs now pass. The first-push 30-minute CI cutoff has already elapsed, so no new wait window is opened. A final PM-only receipt/release commit follows; its exact-head checks remain visible on PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/pull/183 and the branch workflow page. No full-gate success is claimed. All four review findings are fixed; all twelve behavioral reverts failed as expected. Remaining limits: inherited atomic recovery follow-up, pending final CI, and the optional PM timeout-metadata edit refused by the peer-format guard (new links and explicit runner timeout work). Releasing only this agent claim; items remain unclosed. No merge or release."
  "2026-10-27T18:49:37.334Z",codex-agent,"Re-review round 2 accepted. General rule: external values are literal data, never CLI control input; preview and import must share the same representability/mapping boundary. Upstream unbraind/pm-cli#1614 confirms typed PmClient fields also parse sentinels (description/body stdin tokens and assignee clear words). Merged main toolchain update 3064255 first; installed pin is now 2026.10.24. Auditing every package SDK mutation and subprocess boundary, including atomic direct entries, legacy CLI options, capture notes, labels and export. Will use a supported literal/escape path where possible, otherwise refuse before writes with typed unrepresentable_value and a field/remedy. No import may consume process stdin. Existing completed proofs are retained; new tests target literal/sentinel behavior and successful read-back/preview agreement."
  "2026-10-27T19:03:16.786Z",codex-agent,"SDK surface audit: BulkItemMutation create/update rows accept PmClientFullMutationOptions and forward to the same sentinel-parsing lifecycle functions; no literal flag is declared. PmClient create/update likewise expose no literal control. commitImportedItem(document) is available for native import documents but does not preserve the existing bulk transaction/lifecycle contract and is not used to bypass it. Stdin literal WeakMap helpers exist internally but are not exported by the supported SDK runtime, so no deep import or loader bypass was added. Upstream https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1614 is open; follow-up pm-linear-literal-sdk-values tracks adopting its supported fix. Current workaround is explicit typed unrepresentable_value before any item writes for body/description dash and assignee/deadline clear tokens. Due dates are checked as literal calendar dates, preventing relative/control input. Legacy imports now use PmClient directly; atomic and legacy use one SDK option producer, and preview calls the same guarded buildItemPlan. Capture uses structured addJson (not annotation text parsing); export uses JSON GraphQL variables. Earlier final-head CI 40537038689 passed both release gates and both Node jobs, but that older-head success is not evidence for this new fix."
  "2026-10-27T19:25:46.378Z",codex-agent,"Closed the full parser/projection class: the shared literal guard prevents unsupported controls reaching either SDK writer, and the non-atomic path no longer spawns a CLI. Canonicalization alone also misses native lifecycle effects (cancellation clears assignments), so ownership now executes the exact shared atomic update/close rows through a noExtensions PmClient in an owned disposable copy and reads the projected item through the SDK. Copied ownership/closure permissions are bypassed only there; the report never authorizes a real write. Source views are revalidated before hashes are trusted. Focused checks passed 5/5, including caller-stdin preservation, JSON/TOON refusals, leading-dash titles and canceled-role assignment behavior; the source document remained unchanged. Four existing-path regressions also passed, including empty fields, tag encoding and structured comment controls. The earlier packed attempt was stopped after source changed and is not complete evidence; final packed acceptance rebuilds the candidate and enables push-on-write to assert that no provider hook runs from the owned projection. The 500-real-import test is still running; its current process predates the added SDK projection and will be explicitly version-scoped before the final-source rerun."
  "2026-10-27T19:42:16.056Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof completed in independent disposable copies, with production files unchanged: removing only assertLiteralImportValues made the 500-import property fail on a missing expected refusal; restoring the prior previewLinearOwnership raw-option hashing made the SDK lifecycle/projection test fail; restoring the old syncLinearIssues CLI writer made the leading-dash/no-pm test fail. All three exited 1 with assertion failures. Fixed focused checks passed 5/5. The first new property process completed 500 actual imports (250 atomic and 250 non-atomic) plus 179 typed refusal attempts, zero failures, 1613.8 seconds; it predates the final SDK projection and is scoped to the import guard/writer phase. The existing 500-operation model oracle now executes real SDK mutation rows in an independent owned reference tracker and reads native state, instead of merging raw inputs into canonicalDocument. Its isolated 20-operation diagnostic passed; the permanent test remains 500. Native deadline hashes now retain SDK timestamps on both sides, so local time edits cannot disappear through export-only date conversion. Final policy is linear-import-v3-sdk-projection. Final-source 500-import and packed acceptance runs are now in progress; no current full-gate pass is claimed."
  "2026-10-27T20:02:20.942Z",codex-agent,"Coordinator-level closure: the final projection now calls the supported SDK commitItemMutations inside runWithActiveExtensions({path: ownedCopy, noExtensions: true}). This replaces the thin update/close dispatcher, so SDK inspection and skipped-close behavior are shared too; no extension registry or lifecycle rule is reimplemented. The transaction identity includes the current target revision and mutation rows. The copied permissions are bypassed only for the disposable data projection; no authorization or cross-system atomicity is claimed. Fixed coordinator-focused checks passed 5/5, including piped stdin and push-on-write isolation. Source head 63927c5 has passed npm and Bun release gates so far, but that is the preceding dispatcher implementation; the final coordinator change gets fresh CI and packed evidence. Three isolated behavioral revert proofs remain valid and production files were never modified by reverts."
  "2026-10-27T20:13:11.970Z",codex-agent,"Final SDK receipts explicitly limit the projection to native SDK effects: authorization and extension effects remain unvalidated, alongside the no-cross-system-atomicity guarantee. The SDK example retains that guarantee. The coordinator projection uses only supported SDK scope/transaction APIs, with no manual step dispatcher or duplicate input parser. Typecheck, test typecheck and 93-declaration docstrings pass. A final packed rebuild measures this exact receipt text; earlier completed/interrupted artifact runs remain version-scoped. Full source run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40572267404 at 63927c5 passed all four jobs, including npm and Bun release gates. Fresh coordinator run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-linear/actions/runs/40574543609 is in progress; neither older-head result is final-head approval. The first new push cutoff is retained while required independent local acceptance finishes."
